{"evidence":[{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Universal Hartland was the visual effects house of Universal Studios Hollywood.","title":"Universal Hartland Visual Effects"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The effects studio was in operation from 1978 to 1981.","title":"Universal Hartland Visual Effects"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" The studio was created as a means for Universal to enter the visual effects field that was growing larger as well as provide in-house effects creation for "Battlestar Galactica" and "Buck Rogers in the 25th Century".","title":"Universal Hartland Visual Effects"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" Before the facility closed its doors in 1981 it had worked on four films, six television shows (two of which they did effects for the entire run of the show), several Universal Theme Park attractions, some commercials and a few specialty projects, including the special model effects for the Horizons attraction for Disney's Epcot Center and sequences for Disney's Captain EO 3-D attraction.","title":"Universal Hartland Visual Effects"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Captain EO is a 1986 American 3D science fiction film starring Michael Jackson and directed by Francis Ford Coppola (who came up with the name "Captain EO" from the Greek, cf. Eos, the Greek goddess of dawn) that was shown at Disney theme parks from 1986 through 1996.","title":"Captain EO"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The attraction returned to the Disney Parks in 2010 as a tribute after Jackson's death.","title":"Captain EO"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" The film was shown for the final time at Epcot on December 6, 2015.","title":"Captain EO"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Michael Jackson's This Is It (or simply This Is It) is a posthumous two-disc soundtrack album by American singer Michael Jackson.","title":"Michael Jackson's This Is It (album)"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" Released by MJJ Music on October 26, 2009, "This Is It" features previously released music, as well as six previously unreleased recordings by Michael Jackson.","title":"Michael Jackson's This Is It (album)"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" "This Is It" was released to coincide with the theatrical release of "Michael Jackson's This Is It", a concert film documenting Michael Jackson's rehearsals for the This Is It concert series at London's O2 Arena.","title":"Michael Jackson's This Is It (album)"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" "This Is It" is the sixth album to be released by Sony and Motown/Universal since Michael Jackson's death in June 2009.","title":"Michael Jackson's This Is It (album)"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Michael Jackson's Moonwalker is the name of several video games based on the 1988 Michael Jackson film "Moonwalker".","title":"Michael Jackson's Moonwalker"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" U.S. Gold published various games for home computers, released in 1989, whilst Sega developed two similarly themed beat 'em up video games in 1990; one released for arcades and another released for the Mega Drive/Genesis and Master System.","title":"Michael Jackson's Moonwalker"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Each of the games' stories loosely follow the story of the film, in which Michael Jackson must rescue kidnapped children from the evil Mr. Big, and incorporate synthesized versions of some of the musician's songs.","title":"Michael Jackson's Moonwalker"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The Michael Jackson "HIS"tory statue is a sculpture of Michael Jackson created in 1994 by Diana Walczak that became the basis for the cover image of Jackson's album "" as well as the basis for large temporary statues to market the album and the 1995 HIStory World Tour.","title":"Michael Jackson HIStory statue"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" Michael's vision was to appear as a giant statue on the album cover.","title":"Michael Jackson HIStory statue"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Diana sculpted the original statue with a monumental look.","title":"Michael Jackson HIStory statue"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" The sculpture was then digitized, lit, and rendered by her computer animation and visual effects company, Kleiser-Walczak Construction Co., into the "HIStory" album cover.","title":"Michael Jackson HIStory statue"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Manex Visual Effects (MVFX) was a motion picture special visual effects company located in Alameda, California.","title":"Manex Visual Effects"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" Though a small company active only for a short period of time, it provided visual effects for a number of high-profile movies and the company received international recognition including two Best Visual Effects Oscars and one Academy Award for Technical Achievement.","title":"Manex Visual Effects"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" As the company that created Bullet time for The Matrix their work has been highly influential.","title":"Manex Visual Effects"}],"peer_messages":["Unverified peer answer: Francis Ford Coppola
